  "question": {
    "text": "If $7=5+\\frac{1}{7}(5+\\alpha)+\\frac{1}{7^2}(5+2 \\alpha)+\\frac{1}{7^3}(5+3 \\alpha)+\\ldots \\infty$, then the value of $\\alpha$ is :",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "LMIag",
      "text": "$\\frac{6}{7}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GsgxA",
      "text": "6",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "SNTcI",
      "text": "$\\frac{1}{7}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "lqMxj",
      "text": "1",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$S=a+(a+d) r+(a+2 d) r^2+\\ldots$\nThen $S=\\frac{a}{1-r}+\\frac{d r}{(1-r)^2},|r| < 1$\nSince, $r=\\frac{1}{7}$ and $a=5, d=\\alpha$\n$\\begin{aligned}\n& 7=\\frac{5}{1-\\frac{1}{7}}+\\frac{\\alpha \\cdot \\frac{1}{7}}{\\left(1-\\frac{1}{7}\\right)^2} \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow \\alpha=6\n\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
